meta {
  name: Artifacts - Preview
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/artifacts/:artifact/preview
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  artifact: {{artifactId}}
}

params:query {
  ~expires: 
  ~signature: 
}

docs {
  Serves an artifact's bytes inline for display, rather than as the
  attachment `Artifacts - Download` returns.

  **This request will not work as-is.** The endpoint sits outside the
  authenticated group and is protected by a signed URL instead: no bearer
  token, no workspace segment. It answers `403 Invalid or expired
  signature.` unless the `expires` and `signature` query parameters match.

  Don't hand-build those. Take the whole ready-made URL from the
  `preview_url` field of an `Artifacts - Get` or `Artifacts - List`
  response and paste it in — it's a temporary signed route valid for
  15 minutes.

  Only previewable artifacts have a `preview_url` at all: images, HTML,
  PDF, and spreadsheet types (`text/csv`, `.xls`, `.xlsx`). Anything else
  answers `404`.

  The response is the raw file, not the JSON envelope. HTML artifacts are
  served under a `sandbox` Content-Security-Policy and `nosniff`, since
  they're member- and model-supplied bytes coming from the application's
  own origin.
}
